  "verdict": "STAGE E IS NOT A CAPABILITY SCREEN. It passes the ordering checks (1-3) but fails the ones that matter: magnitudes are uncorrelated with accuracy (r=+0.188), it cannot resolve ordered-reverse (p=0.076) which is the one contrast carrying the V1 story, and it fires at p=9e-45 on reverse-baseline, which accuracy says is null. What it measures with enormous power is AUXILIARY-LOSS INTERFERENCE with LM fitting -- every state-carrying arm has higher NLL -- not reasoning capability. Keep it as an interference monitor. It does NOT make B1/B3 answerable on capability.",
